      "body": "@LordHelmchen666 It's a valid question, but I'm waiting a bit to see if the policy change enacted by MaxMind (which was, per their legal team, driven by a desire to comply with GDPR and California's privacy act) causes the other IP geolocation providers to scramble to make similar changes.\r\n\r\nIP2Location, another large supplier of this type of information, is also already behind a login-wall.\r\n\r\nIf they do decide to keep theirs more accessible, we may be able to \"modularize\" how we look for IP geolocation data, and update our attribution message on each page that uses it based on which source we actually found installed.",
